From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 18:29:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09300/11362] Log the root-liveness verifier gap: cell_recall
 1.0 passed an engine nothing can plan in

Offline replay of the goal-defect A/B's banked searches classified all six lp85 cells,
both arms, as model-inert at the planning root: the win predicate was never CONSULTED
(goal_calls = 0), 37 nodes expanded, queue exhausted far under the 20000 budget. The
induced engine produces zero novel successors from the root, and is_level_complete is
only evaluated on novel children, so the search had nowhere to go. Determinism was
proven against a banked plan-True control rather than assumed.

WorldModelVerifier scored these engines at cell_recall 1.0. That is computed over the
induction window's own transitions, so a perfect fit there is compatible with identity
dynamics at the state planning starts from. No existing family scores a model against
the search's entry point, so nothing distinguishes "searched and found nothing" from
"had nowhere to go."

The discriminator is cheap: expand the root under all actions, hash the successors,
count the novel ones. Because it costs a handful of engine calls it can run BEFORE the
search, which makes it a live-path lever rather than a reporting field -- on an unseen
game the agent would learn its model is unusable and re-induce instead of spending its
node budget on a dead engine.

Filed HIGH: it sits upstream of both goal quality and node budget, and on lp85 it made
a primary hit structurally impossible in both arms while every gate read green.

